# Intelligence Layer Blueprint

## Purpose

Define the Field Intelligence functional `I_field[x]`.

## Concept

Field Intelligence measures how well a field configuration:

- maintains structure under perturbation (stability)
- reconfigures under change (adaptability)
- avoids single points of failure (redundancy)
- persists over long time (persistence)

## Example Structure

\[
I_{\text{field}}[x] =
w_1 S_{\text{stab}}[x]
+ w_2 S_{\text{adapt}}[x]
+ w_3 S_{\text{redund}}[x]
+ w_4 S_{\text{persist}}[x]
\]

Where each `S_*` is a scalar metric computed from simulation trajectories.

## Responsibilities

- Define metrics for:
  - stability
  - adaptability
  - redundancy
  - persistence
- Output:
  - scalar `I_field`
  - conceptual gradients wrt `s` and `E_s` (can be approximated)